.TH "LIST-OBJECTS"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
list-objects \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
End of support notice: Beginning October 1, 2025, Amazon S3 will stop returning \fBDisplayName\fP . Update your applications to use canonical IDs (unique identifier for Amazon Web Services accounts), Amazon Web Services account ID (12 digit identifier) or IAM ARNs (full resource naming) as a direct replacement of \fBDisplayName\fP .
.sp
This change affects the following Amazon Web Services Regions: US East (N. Virginia) Region, US West (N. California) Region, US West (Oregon) Region, Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region, Asia Pacific (Sydney) Region, Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Region, Europe (Ireland) Region, and South America (São Paulo) Region.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This operation is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Returns some or all (up to 1,000) of the objects in a bucket. You can use the request parameters as selection criteria to return a subset of the objects in a bucket. A 200 OK response can contain valid or invalid XML. Be sure to design your application to parse the contents of the response and handle it appropriately.
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This action has been revised. We recommend that you use the newer version, \fI\%ListObjectsV2\fP , when developing applications. For backward compatibility, Amazon S3 continues to support \fBListObjects\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following operations are related to \fBListObjects\fP :
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%ListObjectsV2\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetObject\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%PutObject\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%CreateBucket\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%ListBuckets\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.sp
\fBlist\-objects\fP is a paginated operation. Multiple API calls may be issued in order to retrieve the entire data set of results. You can disable pagination by providing the \fB\-\-no\-paginate\fP argument.
When using \fB\-\-output text\fP and the \fB\-\-query\fP argument on a paginated response, the \fB\-\-query\fP argument must extract data from the results of the following query expressions: \fBContents\fP, \fBCommonPrefixes\fP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  list\-objects
\-\-bucket <value>
[\-\-delimiter <value>]
[\-\-encoding\-type <value>]
[\-\-prefix <value>]
[\-\-request\-payer <value>]
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-optional\-object\-attributes <value>]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-starting\-token <value>]
[\-\-page\-size <value>]
[\-\-max\-items <value>]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name of the bucket containing the objects.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- When you use this operation with a directory bucket, you must use virtual\-hosted\-style requests in the format \(ga\(ga \fIBucket\-name\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . Path\-style requests are not supported. Directory bucket names must be unique in the chosen Zone (Availability Zone or Local Zone). Bucket names must follow the format \(ga\(ga \fIbucket\-base\-name\fP \-\-\fIzone\-id\fP \-\-x\-s3\(ga\(ga (for example, \(ga\(ga \fIamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP \-\-\fIusw2\-az1\fP \-\-x\-s3\(ga\(ga ). For information about bucket naming restrictions, see \fI\%Directory bucket naming rules\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBAccess points\fP \- When you use this action with an access point for general purpose buckets, you must provide the alias of the access point in place of the bucket name or specify the access point ARN. When you use this action with an access point for directory buckets, you must provide the access point name in place of the bucket name. When using the access point ARN, you must direct requests to the access point hostname. The access point hostname takes the form \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .s3\-accesspoint.*Region* .amazonaws.com. When using this action with an access point through the Amazon Web Services SDKs, you provide the access point ARN in place of the bucket name. For more information about access point ARNs, see \fI\%Using access points\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Object Lambda access points are not supported by directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBS3 on Outposts\fP \- When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, you must direct requests to the S3 on Outposts hostname. The S3 on Outposts hostname takes the form \(ga\(ga \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .*outpostID* .s3\-outposts.*Region* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, the destination bucket must be the Outposts access point ARN or the access point alias. For more information about S3 on Outposts, see \fI\%What is S3 on Outposts?\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-delimiter\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A delimiter is a character that you use to group keys.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBCommonPrefixes\fP is filtered out from results if it is not lexicographically greater than the key\-marker.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-encoding\-type\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Encoding type used by Amazon S3 to encode the \fI\%object keys\fP in the response. Responses are encoded only in UTF\-8. An object key can contain any Unicode character. However, the XML 1.0 parser can\(aqt parse certain characters, such as characters with an ASCII value from 0 to 10. For characters that aren\(aqt supported in XML 1.0, you can add this parameter to request that Amazon S3 encode the keys in the response. For more information about characters to avoid in object key names, see \fI\%Object key naming guidelines\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When using the URL encoding type, non\-ASCII characters that are used in an object\(aqs key name will be percent\-encoded according to UTF\-8 code values. For example, the object \fBtest_file(3).png\fP will appear as \fBtest_file%283%29.png\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBurl\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-prefix\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Limits the response to keys that begin with the specified prefix.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-request\-payer\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Confirms that the requester knows that she or he will be charged for the list objects request. Bucket owners need not specify this parameter in their requests.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The account ID of the expected bucket owner. If the account ID that you provide does not match the actual owner of the bucket, the request fails with the HTTP status code \fB403 Forbidden\fP (access denied).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-optional\-object\-attributes\fP (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the optional fields that you want returned in the response. Fields that you do not specify are not returned.
.sp
(string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRestoreStatus\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
\(dqstring\(dq \(dqstring\(dq ...
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP | \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP (string)
Reads arguments from the JSON string provided. The JSON string follows the format provided by \fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP\&. If other arguments are provided on the command line, those values will override the JSON\-provided values. It is not possible to pass arbitrary binary values using a JSON\-provided value as the string will be taken literally. This may not be specified along with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&.
.sp
\fB\-\-starting\-token\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A token to specify where to start paginating. This is the \fBNextToken\fP from a previously truncated response.
.sp
For usage examples, see \fI\%Pagination\fP in the \fIAWS Command Line Interface User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-page\-size\fP (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The size of each page to get in the AWS service call. This does not affect the number of items returned in the command\(aqs output. Setting a smaller page size results in more calls to the AWS service, retrieving fewer items in each call. This can help prevent the AWS service calls from timing out.
.sp
For usage examples, see \fI\%Pagination\fP in the \fIAWS Command Line Interface User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-max\-items\fP (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The total number of items to return in the command\(aqs output. If the total number of items available is more than the value specified, a \fBNextToken\fP is provided in the command\(aqs output. To resume pagination, provide the \fBNextToken\fP value in the \fBstarting\-token\fP argument of a subsequent command. \fBDo not\fP use the \fBNextToken\fP response element directly outside of the AWS CLI.
.sp
For usage examples, see \fI\%Pagination\fP in the \fIAWS Command Line Interface User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP (string)
Prints a JSON skeleton to standard output without sending an API request. If provided with no value or the value \fBinput\fP, prints a sample input JSON that can be used as an argument for \fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP\&. Similarly, if provided \fByaml\-input\fP it will print a sample input YAML that can be used with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&. If provided with the value \fBoutput\fP, it validates the command inputs and returns a sample output JSON for that command. The generated JSON skeleton is not stable between versions of the AWS CLI and there are no backwards compatibility guarantees in the JSON skeleton generated.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-debug\fP (boolean)
.sp
Turn on debug logging.
.sp
\fB\-\-endpoint\-url\fP (string)
.sp
Override command\(aqs default URL with the given URL.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fP (boolean)
.sp
By default, the AWS CLI uses SSL when communicating with AWS services. For each SSL connection, the AWS CLI will verify SSL certificates. This option overrides the default behavior of verifying SSL certificates.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-paginate\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatic pagination. If automatic pagination is disabled, the AWS CLI will only make one call, for the first page of results.
.sp
\fB\-\-output\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style for command output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.IP \(bu 2
yaml\-stream
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-query\fP (string)
.sp
A JMESPath query to use in filtering the response data.
.sp
\fB\-\-profile\fP (string)
.sp
Use a specific profile from your credential file.
.sp
\fB\-\-region\fP (string)
.sp
The region to use. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP (string)
.sp
Display the version of this tool.
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fP (string)
.sp
Turn on/off color output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-sign\-request\fP (boolean)
.sp
Do not sign requests. Credentials will not be loaded if this argument is provided.
.sp
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fP (string)
.sp
The CA certificate bundle to use when verifying SSL certificates. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-read\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket read time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket read will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket connect time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket connect will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-binary\-format\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style to be used for binary blobs. The default format is base64. The base64 format expects binary blobs to be provided as a base64 encoded string. The raw\-in\-base64\-out format preserves compatibility with AWS CLI V1 behavior and binary values must be passed literally. When providing contents from a file that map to a binary blob \fBfileb://\fP will always be treated as binary and use the file contents directly regardless of the \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP setting. When using \fBfile://\fP the file contents will need to properly formatted for the configured \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
base64
.IP \(bu 2
raw\-in\-base64\-out
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-pager\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable cli pager for output.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed and configured. See the \fI\%Getting started guide\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP for more information.
.sp
Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix\-like quotation rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal\(aqs quoting rules. See \fI\%Using quotation marks with strings\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following example uses the \fBlist\-objects\fP command to display the names of all the objects in the specified bucket:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3api list\-objects \-\-bucket text\-content \-\-query \(aqContents[].{Key: Key, Size: Size}\(aq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The example uses the \fB\-\-query\fP argument to filter the output of
\fBlist\-objects\fP down to the key value and size for each object
.sp
For more information about objects, see \fI\%Working with Amazon S3 Objects\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 Developer Guide\fP\&.
.SH OUTPUT
.sp
IsTruncated \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A flag that indicates whether Amazon S3 returned all of the results that satisfied the search criteria.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Marker \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates where in the bucket listing begins. Marker is included in the response if it was sent with the request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
NextMarker \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When the response is truncated (the \fBIsTruncated\fP element value in the response is \fBtrue\fP ), you can use the key name in this field as the \fBmarker\fP parameter in the subsequent request to get the next set of objects. Amazon S3 lists objects in alphabetical order.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This element is returned only if you have the \fBdelimiter\fP request parameter specified. If the response does not include the \fBNextMarker\fP element and it is truncated, you can use the value of the last \fBKey\fP element in the response as the \fBmarker\fP parameter in the subsequent request to get the next set of object keys.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Contents \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Metadata about each object returned.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
An object consists of data and its descriptive metadata.
.sp
Key \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name that you assign to an object. You use the object key to retrieve the object.
.sp
Constraints:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
min: \fB1\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
LastModified \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Creation date of the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ETag \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The entity tag is a hash of the object. The ETag reflects changes only to the contents of an object, not its metadata. The ETag may or may not be an MD5 digest of the object data. Whether or not it is depends on how the object was created and how it is encrypted as described below:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Objects created by the PUT Object, POST Object, or Copy operation, or through the Amazon Web Services Management Console, and are encrypted by SSE\-S3 or plaintext, have ETags that are an MD5 digest of their object data.
.IP \(bu 2
Objects created by the PUT Object, POST Object, or Copy operation, or through the Amazon Web Services Management Console, and are encrypted by SSE\-C or SSE\-KMS, have ETags that are not an MD5 digest of their object data.
.IP \(bu 2
If an object is created by either the Multipart Upload or Part Copy operation, the ETag is not an MD5 digest, regardless of the method of encryption. If an object is larger than 16 MB, the Amazon Web Services Management Console will upload or copy that object as a Multipart Upload, and therefore the ETag will not be an MD5 digest.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- MD5 is not supported by directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumAlgorithm \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The algorithm that was used to create a checksum of the object.
.sp
(string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC32\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC32C\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSHA1\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSHA256\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC64NVME\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The checksum type that is used to calculate the object’s checksum value. For more information, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPOSITE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFULL_OBJECT\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Size \-> (long)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Size in bytes of the object
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
StorageClass \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The class of storage used to store the object.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- Directory buckets only support \fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP (the S3 Express One Zone storage class) in Availability Zones and \fBONEZONE_IA\fP (the S3 One Zone\-Infrequent Access storage class) in Dedicated Local Zones.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSTANDARD\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBREDUCED_REDUNDANCY\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGLACIER\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSTANDARD_IA\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBONEZONE_IA\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBINTELLIGENT_TIERING\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDEEP_ARCHIVE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOUTPOSTS\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGLACIER_IR\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSNOW\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFSX_OPENZFS\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Owner \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The owner of the object
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- The bucket owner is returned as the object owner.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
DisplayName \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the display name of the owner. This value is only supported in the following Amazon Web Services Regions:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
US East (N. Virginia)
.IP \(bu 2
US West (N. California)
.IP \(bu 2
US West (Oregon)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Singapore)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Sydney)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Tokyo)
.IP \(bu 2
Europe (Ireland)
.IP \(bu 2
South America (São Paulo)
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ID \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the ID of the owner.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RestoreStatus \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the restoration status of an object. Objects in certain storage classes must be restored before they can be retrieved. For more information about these storage classes and how to work with archived objects, see \fI\%Working with archived objects\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets. Directory buckets only support \fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP (the S3 Express One Zone storage class) in Availability Zones and \fBONEZONE_IA\fP (the S3 One Zone\-Infrequent Access storage class) in Dedicated Local Zones.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IsRestoreInProgress \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether the object is currently being restored. If the object restoration is in progress, the header returns the value \fBTRUE\fP . For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqtrue\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object restoration has completed, the header returns the value \fBFALSE\fP . For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqfalse\(dq, RestoreExpiryDate=\(dq2012\-12\-21T00:00:00.000Z\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object hasn\(aqt been restored, there is no header response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RestoreExpiryDate \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates when the restored copy will expire. This value is populated only if the object has already been restored. For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqfalse\(dq, RestoreExpiryDate=\(dq2012\-12\-21T00:00:00.000Z\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Name \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The bucket name.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Keys that begin with the indicated prefix.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Delimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Causes keys that contain the same string between the prefix and the first occurrence of the delimiter to be rolled up into a single result element in the \fBCommonPrefixes\fP collection. These rolled\-up keys are not returned elsewhere in the response. Each rolled\-up result counts as only one return against the \fBMaxKeys\fP value.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
MaxKeys \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The maximum number of keys returned in the response body.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CommonPrefixes \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
All of the keys (up to 1,000) rolled up in a common prefix count as a single return when calculating the number of returns.
.sp
A response can contain \fBCommonPrefixes\fP only if you specify a delimiter.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBCommonPrefixes\fP contains all (if there are any) keys between \fBPrefix\fP and the next occurrence of the string specified by the delimiter.
.sp
\fBCommonPrefixes\fP lists keys that act like subdirectories in the directory specified by \fBPrefix\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For example, if the prefix is \fBnotes/\fP and the delimiter is a slash (\fB/\fP ), as in \fBnotes/summer/july\fP , the common prefix is \fBnotes/summer/\fP . All of the keys that roll up into a common prefix count as a single return when calculating the number of returns.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for all (if there are any) keys between Prefix and the next occurrence of the string specified by a delimiter. CommonPrefixes lists keys that act like subdirectories in the directory specified by Prefix. For example, if the prefix is notes/ and the delimiter is a slash (/) as in notes/summer/july, the common prefix is notes/summer/.
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the specified common prefix.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
EncodingType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Encoding type used by Amazon S3 to encode the \fI\%object keys\fP in the response. Responses are encoded only in UTF\-8. An object key can contain any Unicode character. However, the XML 1.0 parser can\(aqt parse certain characters, such as characters with an ASCII value from 0 to 10. For characters that aren\(aqt supported in XML 1.0, you can add this parameter to request that Amazon S3 encode the keys in the response. For more information about characters to avoid in object key names, see \fI\%Object key naming guidelines\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When using the URL encoding type, non\-ASCII characters that are used in an object\(aqs key name will be percent\-encoded according to UTF\-8 code values. For example, the object \fBtest_file(3).png\fP will appear as \fBtest_file%283%29.png\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBurl\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RequestCharged \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, indicates that the requester was successfully charged for the request. For more information, see \fI\%Using Requester Pays buckets for storage transfers and usage\fP in the \fIAmazon Simple Storage Service user guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
